projects.description:
Specific activities include: 
- Support the implementation of the National ECD Strategy for 2020-2025 and its Action Plan: intersectoral coordination, monitoring the implementation of the ECD programme, and support the development of the new ECD strategy (MHMI, MOE, MLSP);
- Strengthening parental empowerment by developing evidence- and behavioral-change based solutions to improve pre-school preparation and participation of children in pre-primary education programmes (MoE);
-Promoting positive parenting by strengthening routine services to support responsive caregiving, nurturing care and the well-being of parents (MHMI).

The project "Strengthening Regional Collaboration and National Capacities for Management of Wheat Rust Diseases and Resistance Breeding in Central Asia and Caucasus (CACRust)" has been developed based on the request of the General Directorate of Agricultural Research and Policies (GDAR) of Türkiye. It will serve primarily seven countries in the Central Asia and Caucasus (CAC) region including, Republic of Azerbaijan, Republic of Kazakhstan, Kyrgyz Republic, Republic of Tajikistan, Republic of Türkiye, Turkmenistan and Uzbekistan. Where possible and needed, support will also be provided to additional countries in the Near East and North Africa such as the training and information sharing activities. Other opportunities will also be explored in this regard. For effective implementation of the project, collaborations with the national institutions and international organisations such as Regional Cereal Rust Research Center (RCRRC) based in Izmir, Türkiye, International Center for Agricultural Research in the Dry Areas (ICARDA) and International Wheat and Maize Improvement Center (CIMMYT) will be key. The project activities will complement other activities carried out in context of the Borlaug Global Rust Initiative (BGRI), of which FAO is also a member.

The project will support activities in the following domains: 
I.	Facilitation of regional collaboration and networking;
II.	Training of national technical officers;
III.	Facilitation of disease surveillance;
IV.	Race analysis and mapping through the global rust monitoring system;
V.	Characterization of the resistance properties of the popular varieties;
VI.	Supporting the breeding programmes for developing resistant varieties;
VII.	Integrated disease management;
VIII.	Development of contingency plans and strategies;
IX.	Strengthening physical capacities of institutions.
